{"repositoryId":1259810217,"availability":"available","full":"Daceyyreal/splat-lab","name":"splat-lab","description":"Live in-browser 3D Gaussian Splatting compression — prune, reduce SH, and quantize with a real-time size/quality readout. Companion to splat-slim.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-04T22:07:55Z","updated":"2026-06-14T14:06:02Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://daceyyreal.github.io/splat-lab/","topics":["3d-gaussian-splatting","3d-reconstruction","compression","demo","gaussian-splatting","quantization","threejs","typescript","vite","webgl"],"demo":"https://daceyyreal.github.io/splat-lab/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:18.275Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:18.275Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:18.275Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:18.275Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live, in-browser 3D Gaussian Splatting compression — drag a slider, watch the size and quality change in real time.","splat-lab loads a trained 3DGS .ply in your browser, lets you prune Gaussians, drop spherical-harmonic bands, and quantize — all live — and shows the resulting file size and reduction the moment you move a control. It's the interactive companion to splat-slim: the same compression math, made visual.","The size readout is computed honestly from the field layout and bit widths, so the number you see is the size the model would actually be."],"features":["Opacity prune — drop near-transparent Gaussians by percentile.","Scale cap — remove oversized blobs.","SH degree — reduce spherical harmonics 3 → 2 → 1 → 0 and watch view-dependent color flatten.","Quantization — fp16 / mixed / int8; the int8 setting visibly shows why naive INT8 is risky."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Daceyyreal/splat-lab/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"728b3256c10e7b35971fab4dbf5b4f3e3f7d5c03300e9a0c52a